            <ArticleTitle>[Lumbar spinal stenosis operative treatment--early results].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Early results (12 weeks after surgery) of the lumbar spinal stenosis operative treatment were assessed in the group of 36 patients (aged 40-65 years). In 72% of patients posterior fusion was applied. In the results evaluation lumbar pain, low extremities pain, neurogenic claudicat ion, sensory disturbances and functional status were taken in account. A significant decrease in low extremities and lumbar pain was observed. Some sensory disturbances after operative treatment did not affect general high patients assessment of the performed surgical procedures (positive 80.5% cases).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
